course: dictionary
lesson: 65
title: Acidic: sour and sharp
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Acidic describes something that contains acid, or acts like one. Acidic food and drink tastes sour, like lemons or vinegar. «Rainwater is slightly acidic and slowly dissolves rocks such as limestone.» Here acidic tells you the rain has a little acid in it, which is why it can slowly wear rock away.
explain: Scientists test how acidic a liquid is with indicator paper or red-cabbage water. Acidic liquids turn the paper red or pink, neutral water stays green, and alkaline liquids turn blue or purple. The colour does the telling, so you can use it as a clue when you read about a test.
explain: «An indicator is a substance whose colour shows whether something is acidic or alkaline.» The words around acidic show it is one of two opposites, acidic or alkaline. To check your meaning, swap it in: an acidic liquid has a pH lower than 7, so the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Acidic means containing acid, or acting like an acid.
fact: In science, an acidic liquid has a pH lower than 7.
fact: «Acidic» food or drink tastes sour, like lemons or vinegar.
fact: Acidic drinks can harm tooth enamel, which is the hard outer layer of your teeth.
fact: Acid rain and acidic soil are phrases you may meet in science and geography.
exercise: «Rainwater is slightly acidic and slowly dissolves rocks.» What does acidic mean? | *Contains a little acid | Very sweet and sugary | Frozen solid | Full of soil
exercise: Ella tests a liquid with red-cabbage water and it turns pink. What does that suggest? | It is neutral and stays green | It is alkaline and blue | It is sweet to taste | *It is acidic
exercise: Which everyday item is acidic because it tastes sour? | *Vinegar | Sugar | Plain water | Ice cube
test: On indicator paper, which colour does neutral water stay? | Blue | Pink | Red | *Green
test: «Seeds cannot grow in your stomach, which is dark, very acidic and has no soil.» What does very acidic mean here? | Cool and wet | *Full of strong acid | Sweet and sugary | Full of soil
exam: In science, which pH value shows that a liquid is acidic? | pH 10 | *pH 4 | pH 12 | pH 7
